  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Changed\n\n- **Lowered the `Uno.WinUI` floor from 6.7.103 to 6.6.184.** `Pysar.Uno` previously\n  demanded a version no app on `Uno.Sdk 6.6.42` could satisfy — the Sdk supplies\n  6.6.184 itself, making the higher floor a hard resolution failure rather than a\n  warning. `Pysar.Uno` uses no API newer than 6.6, so the floor now matches.\n- This is a floor, not a ceiling: consumers on `Uno.Sdk 6.7.30` still resolve\n  6.7.135, and the Uno sample builds against 6.8.0-dev.159 from its own Sdk.\n- `HarfBuzzSharp` remains at 14.2.1.1 — only its outdated rationale comment was\n  corrected, since `Svg.Skia` (14.2.0), not Uno, is what drives that version now.\n\n### Notes\n\n- Apps blocked on `Uno.WinUI 6.7.103` can now stay on Uno 6.6 — or move to\n  `Uno.Sdk 6.7.30`, which is published as stable.",
